{"body":"This branch now treats a checkpoint as \"already migrated\" whenever its `/full/*` artifacts are present, but it no longer checks whether `/main` still lacks `transcript.jsonl`. That means rerunning the migration will skip older v2 checkpoints that have raw transcripts archived but are still missing the compact transcript on `/main`, so the previous backfill/repair path is gone unless the user does a full `--force` rewrite.","created_at":"2026-05-05T00:28:22Z","id":3185316743,"line":329,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"This new read path bypasses `wrapWithFetcher`, unlike the existing v1 `ReadSessionMetadata` and the other v2 readers in this file. On treeless/partial clones or when go-git's object cache is stale, `metadata.json` can be present on disk but unavailable through `sessionTree.File()`; in that case migration reruns will now fail here even though the older `ReadSessionMetadataAndPrompts` path could recover the blob via `git cat-file` or the configured fetcher.","created_at":"2026-05-05T00:28:22Z","id":3185316772,"line":null,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_read.go","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"Gating the repair pass on `freshlyPackedRefs` means a normal rerun no longer fixes stale `generation.json` in already-migrated repos. This helper is only invoked from `migrate.go`, so if the repo has archived refs with bad metadata but nothing new to pack, `entire migrate --checkpoints v2` now exits without any way to repair those archives.\n","created_at":"2026-05-05T00:28:22Z","id":3185316786,"line":null,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"This might be a purely stylistic choice so feel free to ignore this comment.\n\nThe role of `indexFullSessionsInTree` within `BuildFullSessionArtifactsIndex` is a bit odd to me: We're creating `index` in this function only to have it mutated by `indexFullSessionsInTree`. That isn't what I would have expected.\n\nI'm wondering if it would be easier to read/understand to have a function `listFullSessionsInTree()` return a list of sessions per ref and merge them into the tree in `BuildFullSessionArtifactsIndex()` to avoid passing an object around and mutating it in multiple places which imo makes following the data flow harder than it needs to be.","created_at":"2026-05-05T20:54:19Z","id":3191511010,"line":182,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go","user":"pfleidi"}
{"body":"Given that this acts like a Set, could this be a `map[string]bool`?","created_at":"2026-05-05T20:56:05Z","id":3191520044,"line":142,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go","user":"pfleidi"}
{"body":"Part of me is wondering whether the split between `migrateCheckpointsV2` and `migrateCheckpointsV2Internal` is necessary. Could we inline the code changes here and update the signature of `migrateCheckpointsV2()` instead?","created_at":"2026-05-05T21:13:50Z","id":3191607923,"line":204,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go","user":"pfleidi"}

